# scry-on-turn at turn 1, three cards: "At the beginning of your upkeep, if it's your first turn, scry 3." Bot1 plays first,
# so its first upkeep is turn 1's: it looks at the top three (CR 701.22a), keeps the Plains on top and puts the Island and
# the Mountain on the bottom, and draws the Plains on turn 3. Bot2's first upkeep (turn 2) and Bot1's second (turn 3) have
# no trigger: the turn is the wearer's own, and its first.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest x7
Island
Mountain
Plains
Forest x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Variant]
Bot1: maximum 20; emblem Gear test: scry-on-turn, turn 1, count 3

[Actions]
[T1 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack = Gear test: scry-on-turn, turn 1, count 3
Bot1.Arrange(Plains | Island; Mountain)
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Plains
Bot1.Library.Count = 32
